This dossier supports first-time, never-licensed applicants preparing for the West Virginia Class E knowledge examination. The issuing authority is the West Virginia Division of Motor Vehicles within the West Virginia Department of Transportation, and the source is the current revised edition of the West Virginia Driver's Licensing Handbook pinned in the run configuration. The registrar verified no official question count, passing score, test format or time limit for the knowledge examination, so this dossier asserts no value for any of them. The handbook's own examination chapter describes a question minimum and a passing line in its text; those lines travel only as cited knowledge facts in the knowledge-examination section of this run, never as verified exam facts. Practice scoring follows only the accepted LearningLoop product policy. Section Eight covers railroad crossing signs and signals, every traffic light indication from circular green through the red arrow and the turn-on-red rules, intersection flashers, lane use control signals, crosswalk signals and the blind pedestrian's right-of-way, and the pavement markings from yellow and white lines through diamond lanes, center left-turn lanes, reversible lanes, crosswalk lines and stop lines.
